-- title:
--   Galois conjugation of Atkin–Lehner q-expansions as a diamond operator
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \nmid M$, an even integer $k$, and a modular form $f$ of weight $k$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, regarded as a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$. Assume $f$ has integral $q$-expansion in the sense of [`ModularCurve.IsIntegralQExp`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L37): there is a power series $p_0$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the period-$1$ $q$-expansion of $f$. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M)$ with $p \mid \gamma_{11}$, let $K \subset \mathbb{C}$ be the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta)$ generated by $\zeta = e^{2\pi i/p}$, let $b$ be a natural number coprime to $p$, and let $\varphi : K \to \mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism sending any element of $K$ whose complex value is $\zeta$ to $\zeta^{b}$. Let $\delta \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ with $\delta_{00} \equiv b \pmod p$ and $\delta_{00} \equiv 1 \pmod M$. Then for every natural number $n$ there is $z \in K$ whose complex value is the $n$-th coefficient of the period-$1$ $q$-expansion of $\tau \mapsto (f \mid_k \gamma)(p\tau)$, where $p\tau$ is the action of [`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix p`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21), the upper-triangular matrix $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$, and the $n$-th coefficient of the period-$1$ $q$-expansion of $\tau \mapsto ((f \mid_k \delta) \mid_k \gamma)(p\tau)$ equals $\varphi(z)$.
--
--   This is the Shimura reciprocity statement for $q$-expansions at the Atkin–Lehner matrix $\gamma\,\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$ at $p$: conjugating the expansion of $f \mid W_p$ by the automorphism $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{b}$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ has the same effect as precomposing $f$ with a matrix $\delta$ representing the diamond operator attached to $b$. It is used, in the form with an abstract field automorphism in place of the embedding $\varphi$, in the analysis of the Galois action on expansions of forms of level $Mp$ at the cusps above $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_qExpansion_coeff_atkinLehnerSlash_eq_and_slash_mul_eq_apply_gamma1_mul.lean

